# MCP mutating tool responses

When adding or changing tools under `mcp-server/`:

1. Mutating tools **must** return via `ok` / `fail` / `actionRequired` from `mcp-server/lib/respond.ts` (or re-exports from `page-tool-helpers.ts`). Do not return ad-hoc `{ content: [...] }` success payloads from mutating handlers.
2. Before shipping a mutate tool, document **side effects**, **warnings** (what does not happen), and **intended follow-ups**.
3. Populate `next_actions` whenever another tool call is needed for correctness. Use `[]` only when nothing useful remains.
4. Always include `warnings: []` (or populated). Use warnings for non-propagation facts (especially variants/promote) — do not bury those only in `message` prose.
5. `tool` names in `next_actions` must be real registered MCP tool names; never invent tools (no `validate_content`, etc.).
6. Do not add server-side **locale** fan-out for MCP; guide agents with `next_actions` instead. Loopback calls set `x-mcp-author` so the main app skips shared-layout fan-out.
7. **Shared layout:** one tool set only. Detect shared layout; use `layout_target` / `action_required: confirm_layout_target` when ambiguous; never invent parallel `*_shared` tools.
8. **Shared template (`type_single`) writes:** `reason` must state shared template + blast radius + sibling structure rules. Prefer `sharedStructuralEnvelope` / sibling helpers in `shared-layout.ts`.
9. **Section bindings:** single-section live `update_fields` edits propagate on the server (`bound_updates`). Multi-section `updates[]` are rejected (`split_section_updates`). Variant edits: warn via `warnings` (`variant_no_binding_propagate`).
10. When known, put **concrete relative file paths** (and what does **not** happen: listings vs page, variants, locale fan-out) in `warnings` and/or `side_effects`, not only in free-form `message`. Prefer typed `side_effects[].paths` (`McpSideEffect.paths`) for those file paths. Top-level ok-payload `paths` on some tools (e.g. detach/reattach) is a separate field — do not conflate it with `side_effects[].paths`.
11. Prefer **dense structured** education over long prose; do not drop facts to be brief. Staff UI may be more verbose; MCP should stay efficient with no loss.
12. Inspection/read tools that only report state should use `next_actions: []` unless a follow-up is required for correctness (e.g. `get_entry_fields` always returns `[]`).
13. **Section property paths on ecommerce/CTA validation:** agent-facing failures (`actionRequired` / `details` / `warnings`) **must include exact section property path(s)** when known (e.g. `sections[2].data.ecommerce_products`, `programs[].id`, `signup_card.cta_button.tracking`, or `_ecommerce.yml` `funnel.steps`) — not only prose like “missing product scope.” `next_actions` remain real MCP tool names; the property path lives in `message` / `details` / `warnings` / `property_path`.
14. **Agent changelog:** When changing MCP tools, explain docs (`mcp-server/explain/`), envelopes, tool catalog gates, or other agent-facing contracts, **append** an entry to [`mcp-server/agent-changelog.yml`](mcp-server/agent-changelog.yml) (`date` ISO day, `summary`, 1–3 `agent_impact` bullets, optional `paths`, set `tools_changed: true` when tools are added/removed/renamed). `get_agent_changelog` serves only the last **6 days** (filter at read). Remind humans to refresh/reconnect the MCP connector when the tool list changes — agents cannot refresh `tools/list` mid-session.
